{
  "schema": "plainsong-notes-variants-gold-v1",
  "description": "Meaning annotations for notes-variants-holdout-r2-fixtures.json, in the format of notes-variants-gold.json, plus three fields per family. labels lists exact spoken heading or recording-label phrases that name the recording or an agenda section, never a person, deliverable or product. numbers lists every quantity and price (not calendar dates): value is the canonical digit string, terms are lowercase prefixes of the noun, subject and modifiers the number is attached to in its own source clause, and restriction lists prefixes that a correct restatement of that number must keep (empty when unrestricted). actors maps each person to the verb prefixes that person may correctly be the grammatical subject of: their own commitments, conditions they are the subject of, actions the source says they did, and speech acts they actually performed. Every term is attested as a prefix of a canonicalized word in its meeting's source text. Dates use canonical forms; a spoken correction leaves only the corrected date.",
